-- title:
--   Transport of chart-pole and other-pole clauses along the level-field identification
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 2$, $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell_g$ is a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Further data: a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` for which $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`, the predicate `LiesOverPrime`); a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (the subfield of Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by $j$ and $j(\mathsf q^{M'})$), with `hW` asserting that $W$ is exactly the set of places satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace q M'`; a distinguished element $s \in W$; the inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise images of the full modular function field of level $M'$) into `fieldBar q M'` (the corresponding base change of the $X_H$-function field of level $q^2M'$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'`); and a constant reduction $R_0$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $A$, i.e. a valuation subring `R₀.integers` with a surjective residue homomorphism onto the latter field, cutting $A$ out of the constants, degree-preserving on places and compatible with orders of vanishing. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that every Laurent series over $A$ whose coefficientwise image over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers` and has $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise reduction of that series modulo the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   On the base-field side there are an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$; write $A_0 :=$ `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` for the induced valuation subring of $k_0$. The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`, `hκ` state that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, Henselian, with algebraically closed residue field, and that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$. An auxiliary block of arithmetic data consists of a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ that is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ and satisfying $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ with $u$ a unit of $A$; an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$ together with a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ induced by $A$ (`hAb`) whose maximal ideal is generated by a non-zero $\varpi_b$; the tameness hypothesis `htame` that $(\ell_g-1)/2$ is a unit of $A_0$; and $\xi \in k_0$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity.
--
--   The level structure is given by $H_1 =$ `levelH q M'` $\cap \ker\big((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times\big)$ (`hH₁`) and by $K_\ell$, an intermediate field of $(\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0)/k_0$ equal to `laurentBaseChange k₀ (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)` (`hKℓ`), carrying an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $k_0$; an element $j_\ell \in K_\ell$, non-zero, with $j_\ell =$ `coeffEmb k₀ jq` (`hjℓ`); an element $\varpi_t' \in A_0$ with $\varpi_t' = \varpi_t$ (`hϖt'`) and a natural number $m \ge 1$ with $\pi_0^m = \varpi_t' w$ for some unit $w$ of $A_0$ (`hm`, `hm1`). Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A₀ Kℓ jℓ` for the subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$. Further data: a maximal ideal $y$ of $C$ containing $\pi_0$ (`hy`, `hϖy`); an $A_0$-subalgebra $B_t$ of $K_\ell$ and a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ with $B_t \subseteq W_t$ (`hBW`); natural numbers $n \ge 1$ with $n \mid q+1$; $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ lying in $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau_0 \in \mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ with `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ₀⁻¹ Kℓ τ₀` (the $q$-expansion identity which says that $\tau_0$ realises the action of $\gamma_0^{-1}$ on ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms on $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, normalised by $\xi \mapsto e^{2\pi i/q}$) and with $W_t$ stable under $\tau_0$ (`hτ₀W`); an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ with $\zeta_c^{\,n} = 1$ and $\zeta_c^{\,k}-1$ a unit for $0 < k < n$; the element `jqNModC k₀ q` of $K_\ell$ (`hjK`), which lies in $C$ (`hjC`) and is congruent modulo $y$ to a constant $a_0 \in A_0$ (`ha₀y`); a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$; and the equality `hn`: $n =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, the quotient of `jWidthChar q` of the value of $s$ at `jGeomGen` by `placeRamificationJ M' s`.
--
--   The supersingularity and position hypotheses are: `hss`, that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the image of $j_\ell$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`, the set of $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic curves have trivial $q$-torsion; `hover`, that $y$ is the point of the chart lying over $s$, in the sense that for every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-image lies in `R₀.integers`, which is regular at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which $j$ is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the element `coeffEmb k₀ g` of $C$ differs from any constant $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose $A$-residue equals $s$ evaluated at that $R_0$-residue by an element of $y$; and `hOrbit`, that every maximal ideal $y'$ of $C$ containing $\pi_0$ and satisfying this same centring condition is the transport of $y$ along some $\tau$ attached, in the sense of `IsLevelAutAt`, to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, with $\tau$ preserving $C$.
--
--   The remaining hypotheses are large conjunctions, summarised here. `hS1` asserts: $C \subseteq B_t$; $K_\ell$ is the fraction field of $B_t$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$, with $B_t/\pi_0$ of Krull dimension at most $1$; $W_t$ meets $k_0$ in exactly $A_0$, has maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is a discrete valuation ring, cuts out $y$ on $C$, and is the localisation of $B_t$ at its maximal ideal; for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $\kappa$ of $A_0$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B_t$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) whose kernel is the set of elements of $B_t$ in the maximal ideal of $W_t$, which is compatible with constants, and which is equivariant for level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ through the action [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) of an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), with $c \ne 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity, and with a further level automorphism realising the pair $(1, c)$; $B_t$ is stable under all level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is obtained from the maximal ideal of $W_t$ by such a level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; and an element of $B_t$ carried into the maximal ideal of $W_t$ by all such automorphisms is divisible by $\pi_0$. `hR7` asserts: $\tau_0$ has exact order $n$ in its action on $B_t$, and every level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with a power of $\tau_0$; `ends` has exactly $q+1$ elements, is permuted by the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ that preserve $W_t$, transitively so, each member being stable under $\tau_0$, and distinct members are separated by an element that is a unit in one and not in the other; there is a finite-type $A_0$-subalgebra $B_c$ of $K_\ell$, stable under the level automorphisms with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, contained in every member of `ends`, each member being a localisation of $B_c$; each $O \in$ `ends` is contained in $W_t$, is local and Noetherian, contains $C$, meets $k_0$ in exactly $A_0$, and every element of $O$ is congruent to a constant in the sense that a suitable difference fails to be a unit; the adic completion of each $O$ is isomorphic over the completion of $A_0$ to the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` at $\pi_0^m$, with elements $c_x, c_y$ mapping to unit multiples of the distinguished elements $U$ and $V$ and satisfying $c_xc_y = \pi_0^m \cdot(\text{unit})$, with constants matching `UVCrossingModel.const`, with $c_y$ in and $c_x$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$, with `jqNModC k₀ q` $- a_0$ corresponding to a unit multiple of $V^e$ for some $e \ge 1$, and with $\tau_0$ corresponding to an automorphism $\theta_0$ which multiplies $U$ by $\zeta_c$ and $V$ by $\zeta_c^{-1}$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal; each $O$ moreover carries a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_\ell$ containing $O$ and $C$, with constants $A_0$, a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $\pi_0$, in which a parameter $t$ and `jqNModC k₀ q` are residually transcendental over $A_0$, in which $c_x$ lies in and $c_y$ lies outside the maximal ideal, which cuts out exactly $y$ on $C$, and which separates $O$ from the other members of `ends`, also under level automorphisms; and each $O$ carries a finite-type $A_0$-subalgebra $B_x$ of $B_t \cap O$, stable under level automorphisms with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, whose elements are regular at every place of $K_\ell/k_0$ at which $j_\ell$ is regular, with $O$ the localisation of $B_x$, and containing an element lying outside every valuation subring with constants $A_0$, with $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal, with $j_\ell$ residually transcendental, and not containing $O$; finally every valuation subring of $K_\ell$ with constants $A_0$ which contains $C$ and cuts out $y$ on $C$ either contains $B_t$ or dominates one of the members of `ends`. `hR9` asserts that some $b \in B_t$ lies outside every valuation subring of $K_\ell$ with constants $A_0$ in which $\pi_0$ is a non-unit and $j_\ell$ is residually transcendental (no monic polynomial over $A_0$ evaluated at $j_\ell$ falls into the maximal ideal). `hR10` asserts that for every maximal ideal $y''$ of $C$ containing $\pi_0$ which is not the transport of $y$ under any level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, some $b \in B_t$ lies outside every valuation subring of $K_\ell$ containing $C$ in which the $\tau$-pullback of $y''$ lands in the maximal ideal, for all such $\tau$.
--
--   Finally, $G$ is the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ generated by the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, $K_0$ is its fixed field, $B_0$ is the subalgebra of $G$-invariants of $B_t$, and $W_0'$ is the valuation subring of $K_0$ obtained by intersecting with $W_t$.
--
--   With $\overline{F} :=$ `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \overline F$, the assertion is the following. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline F/k_0$ consisting exactly of those $f$ all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $k_0$, and let $\varphi : K_0 \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } F_0$ be a $k_0$-algebra isomorphism satisfying: the coefficientwise image along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ of every $f \in K_0$ equals $\varphi f$ as a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\xi' \in k_0$ with $\zeta$ the image of $\xi'$, and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ' q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ Kℓ τ`, the field $K_0$ is $\tau$-stable and $\varphi$ carries $\tau|_{K_0}$ to `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; and for every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ with `coeffEmb k₀ g` in $K_\ell$ and in $K_0$, $\varphi$ sends it to the image under the inclusion `hle` of the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-coefficientwise image of $g$. Let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $F_0$ obtained as the preimage of $W_0'$ under $\varphi^{-1}$, and let $B$ be the subring of $\overline F$ consisting of the images under $\varphi$, followed by $F_0 \hookrightarrow \overline F$, of the elements of $K_0$ whose image in $K_\ell$ lies in $B_0$.
--
--   Assume the two upstairs separation clauses. First, that there exists $b \in K_0$ with image in $B_0$ such that $b \notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ which meets $k_0$ exactly in $A$ (an element of $k_0$ lies in $A$ if and only if its image lies in $V$), in which $\pi_0$ lies in the maximal ideal, and in which the element `coeffEmb k₀ jq` of $K_0$ lies and is residually transcendental over the constants (no monic polynomial over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$, evaluated there, lies in the maximal ideal of $V$). Second, that for every $s' \in W$ with $s' \ne s$ there exists $b \in K_0$ with image in $B_0$ such that $b \notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ with the same constants condition which is centred at $s'$, in the sense that for every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-image lies in `R₀.integers`, which is regular wherever $j$ is, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s'$, the element `coeffEmb k₀ g` lies in $K_0$ and in $V$, and its difference with any constant $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose $A$-residue is $s'$ evaluated at that residue lies in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   The conclusion is the conjunction of the two corresponding clauses downstairs. First: there exists $b \in \overline F$ lying in $F_0$ and in $B$ such that, for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ meeting $k_0$ exactly in $A$, in which $\pi_0$ lies in the maximal ideal, and in which the image under `hle` of the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-coefficientwise image of $jq$ lies and is residually transcendental over the constants (no monic polynomial over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$, evaluated at it, lies in the maximal ideal), the element $b$ of $F_0$ does not lie in $V$. Second: for every $s' \in W$ with $s' \ne s$ there exists $b \in \overline F$ lying in $F_0$ and in $B$ such that, for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ meeting $k_0$ exactly in $A$ and centred at $s'$ — meaning that for every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-image lies in `R₀.integers`, which is regular at every place at which $j$ is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s'$, the image of that $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-image under `hle` lies in $F_0$ and in $V$, and its difference with any constant $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose $A$-residue is $s'$ evaluated at that residue lies in the maximal ideal of $V$ — the element $b$ of $F_0$ does not lie in $V$.
--
--   This is the transport step, along the identification $\varphi$ of the fixed field $K_0$ of the level-automorphism group with the intermediate field $F_0$ of the level-$q^2M'$ function field cut out by having $k_0$-rational $q$-expansion coefficients, of the two separation clauses used to pin down the supersingular point $s$: the clause excluding the valuation subrings at which $j$ stays residually transcendental (the chart pole) and the clause excluding the valuation subrings centred at the other supersingular places of $W$. It is the $q = 2$, $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-frame form of that step, and it feeds the assembly statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
